# Cloudflare redirect rules for the deployed artefact.
#
# Astro copies this file verbatim from public/ to the root of dist/.
#
# The playground is a single-page application: its client-side routes exist only
# once Blazor is running, so a cold request to one of them must be answered with
# the application shell rather than a 404. The rewrite below does that, and it is
# a rewrite (status 200), not a redirect — the visitor's URL has to survive, or
# the router has nothing left to route on when it starts.
#
# ORDERING ASSUMPTION, to be confirmed on the first real preview: static assets
# are matched before these rules, so /playground/_framework/... keeps being served
# as itself rather than being swallowed by the splat. If that turns out to be
# false, the runtime will 404 in a way no local static server reproduces, and this
# rule needs narrowing to the routes the application actually declares.
/playground/*  /playground/index.html  200
